Reason: in the mine room (rm_a5c22) a power bomb sets off a chain of mines, each throwing 108 projectiles: ~1,000
projectiles at once, crowded into the same grid cells. firstCollisionHit (patch 0056) then found the cells fuller than
the target's own instance list and fell back to the full sorted walk for almost every projectile (984 a frame on the
Wii): ~20,000 pair tests a frame at ~0.34 µs, ~14 ms a frame, though only ~34 collisions fire. In that case it now
looks for the first hit in the target's list itself, unsorted, as it already does in the grid cells, so the sorted
walk starts at that hit or is skipped when nothing hits. The list's boxes are worked out once per box epoch (a counter
moved by every dirty mark and every removal from the per-object lists; every write to a box input marks dirty) and
shared by all the selves that ask, so only members whose box meets self's go through the pair's full tests. A pair's
boxes are also compared before its collision target is resolved (all its tests must pass and none changes anything).
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

